What is vendored, and why
-------------------------
Copied unmodified from the package's es5/ tree, paths preserved:

  es5/tex-mml-chtml.js                 combined component (loader, startup,
                                       core, TeX + MathML input, CHTML output,
                                       ui/menu, a11y/assistive-mml)
  es5/output/chtml/fonts/woff-v2/*     CHTML web fonts (loaded via @font-face
                                       from [mathjax]/output/chtml/fonts/woff-v2)
  es5/input/tex/extensions/*           every TeX extension; targets of the
                                       autoload / require / noerrors loads

MathJax derives [mathjax] from its own script URL, so in the preview these
are requested from x-macdown-asset:///<bundle>/Contents/Resources/MathJax/es5/.

Deliberately NOT vendored: a11y/{explorer,complexity,semantic-enrich,sre}.js,
sre/ (speech rule engine, ~3.8 MB, which also fetches JSON and so would need
a CSP connect-src), output/svg*, ui/{lazy,safe}.js, input/mml/extensions,
input/asciimath. All of these are requested only from MathJax's contextual
menu, which init.js disables in the preview (options.enableMenu). Hidden
assistive MathML for screen readers is part of the combined component and
stays on.

MacDown's own file: init.js (configuration; not part of MathJax).

Updating
--------
Re-download the tarball, verify it against `dist.integrity` from
https://registry.npmjs.org/mathjax/<version>, copy the same three paths,
recompute the sha384 of es5/tex-mml-chtml.js, confirm the jsDelivr copy is
byte-identical, and update kMPMathJaxCDN / kMPMathJaxCDNIntegrity in
MPRenderer.m and this file.
